        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.087,
            0.255,
            0.106
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 101.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.119,
            0.648,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": "？ **What are these numbers in Step 3 and Step 4? Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.159,
            0.608,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "Step 3: No. of matchsticks placed horizontally-3 No. of matchsticks placed diagonally-4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.212,
            0.608,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "Step 4: No. of matchsticks placed horizontally-4 No. of matchsticks placed diagonally-5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.265,
            0.883,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "？ **How does the number of matchsticks change in each orientation as the steps increase? Write an expression for the number of matchsticks at Step ‘y’ in each orientation. Do the two expressions add up to 2y + 1?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.344,
            0.2,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.377,
            0.53,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "For horizontal placement: 1, 2, 3, 4, …"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.399,
            0.719,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "At the yth step, the number of horizontal matchsticks = y."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.422,
            0.514,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "For diagonal placement: 2, 3, 4, 5, …"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.443,
            0.736,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": "At the yth step, the number of diagonal matchsticks = **y + 1**. Yes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.502,
            0.255,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 102.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.525,
            0.293,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it Out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.553,
            0.883,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "**1. One plate of Jowar roti costs ₹30 and one plate of Pulao costs ₹20. If x plates of Jowar roti and y plates of pulao were ordered in a day, which expression(s) describe the total amount in rupees earned that day? (a) 30x + 20y** (b) $\\begin{aligned} &(30 + 20) \\times (x + y)\\\\ &30x - 20y\\\\ \\end{aligned}$ **(c) 20x + 30y** (d) $(30 + 20) \\times x + y$ (e)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.665,
            0.297,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (a) 30x + 20y."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.701,
            0.883,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": "**2. Pushpita sells two types of flowers on Independence Day: champak and marigold. ‘p’ customers only bought champak, ‘q’ customers only bought marigold, and ‘r’ customers bought both. On the same day, she gave away a tiny national flag to every customer. How many flags did she give away that day?** (a) $\\pmb { p } + \\pmb { q } + \\pmb { r }$ (b) $\\pmb { p } + \\pmb { q } + 2 \\pmb { r }$ (c) $2 \\times ( \\boldsymbol{p} + \\boldsymbol{q} + \\boldsymbol{r} )$ (d) $p + q + r + 2$ (e) $\\boldsymbol{p}+\\boldsymbol{q}+\\boldsymbol{r}+\\boldsymbol{1}$ (f) $2 \\times ( \\pmb { p } + \\pmb { q } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.867,
            0.282,
            0.885
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (a) $p + q + r$"
        },
        {
